        "original_id": "9d930d65-3d94-503e-8b7b-48ae86314007",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport, Louisville International Airport, Staunton, Augusta County, Virginia, Louisville, Jefferson County, Kentucky, Grottoes\n- Products: Henson Airlines Flight 1517\n- Concepts: airport codes, general aviation, commercial airline service, public airports, military-use airports, air crash approach\n\nFacts:\n- On September 23, 1985, Henson Airlines Flight 1517 crashed in Grottoes, Virginia, while approaching Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport.\n- Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport has the codes IATA SHD, ICAO KSHD, and FAA LID SHD.\n- Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport is a public airport 10 nautical miles northeast of Staunton in Augusta County, Virginia, United States.\n- Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport is used mostly for general aviation and is also served by one commercial airline.\n- Louisville International Airport has the codes IATA SDF, ICAO KSDF, and FAA LID SDF.\n- Louisville International Airport is a public and military-use public airport centrally located in Louisville in Jefferson County, Kentucky, United States.",
